{"id": "EUVD-2026-81994", "enisaUuid": "f6c3567c-31a4-301e-84a9-83b86bf11e3e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-integrity: replace forgeable discard filler with a keyed sector marker\n\nThe discard-block check in dm_integrity_rw_tag() treats a stored tag\nof all 0xf6 bytes (DISCARD_FILLER) as proof a block was discarded and\nskips HMAC verification. allow_discards is only accepted in\ndm-integrity's standalone mode. An attacker with raw write access to\nthe backing device, but without the integrity key, can stamp any block\nwith an all-0xf6 tag and have it served as authentic.\n\nAdd a new \"allow_discards_keyed\" target argument that marks discarded\nblocks with a keyed checksum of (salt || sector) instead, computed by\nintegrity_discard_checksum().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/388c3f6496bb8083576d989e6d249ba9807c6b0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c58ea19a909ef6bed4f0f824e9cd7e30d7e4775", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6228722c27304e4682cddc1fede03898f87e4414", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68c5c42567bc462139128968ebbfadd0aefff519"], "aliases": ["GHSA-62c9-4g59-6rj6", "CVE-2026-90333"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16865f29-ae31-3a7a-85c6-174591ac0850", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "84597a44a9d86ac949900441cea7da0af0f2f473 <68c5c42567bc462139128968ebbfadd0aefff519"}, {"id": "177445f6-8b35-30ab-80f9-e98e3ef2c30a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "84597a44a9d86ac949900441cea7da0af0f2f473 <388c3f6496bb8083576d989e6d249ba9807c6b0b"}, {"id": "1af9867d-86cc-383c-a44d-dfc6bd768c07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "1ef90fad-3e70-3f10-aec3-36c7301d1955", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"